+# Mobile in-app notification preferences
+
+Apply `mobile-notification-preferences.patch` after `mobile-document-viewing.patch` and the seven preceding version-4 mobile patches on clean backend `42b4552`. Run Prisma generate and migrate deploy before restarting the API. The additive migration adds three Boolean columns to beneficiary_mobile_accounts, defaulting to true for existing and new accounts. No backend/mobile dependency is added.
+
+GET/PATCH `/api/v1/mobile/beneficiaries/me/notification-preferences` requires an active beneficiary mobile session. The response contains only `{ enrollmentUpdates, scheduleUpdates, claimUpdates }`. PATCH requires all three strict Booleans and rejects unknown/owner/delivery fields. The owner comes from the session; the save rechecks and locks the active session/account inside its audit transaction. Responses are private/no-store.
+
+`createMobileNotifications` reads these preferences in the staff action's transaction before creating future automatic IN_APP messages. Enrollment events use enrollmentUpdates, SCHEDULE_PUBLISHED uses scheduleUpdates, and claim verification/release/simulated credit/reversal use claimUpdates. A beneficiary without a mobile account retains the prior default behavior. Existing messages and read timestamps remain intact; re-enabling does not backfill suppressed events. Deduplication and transaction rollback remain in force. Staff broadcasts/manual delivery queues and authentication codes are outside this preference scope.
+
+Mobile replaces the preview SMS/push switches with these saved in-app settings. It handles loading/retry, keeps failed edits, blocks repeated saves and discards results after account changes. The original port-3000 API shows unavailable instead of fake settings. No device push registration, remote push sender, SMS reminder delivery or permission prompt is added. Android remote push requires an Expo development/release build, Expo project/FCM credentials and device delivery validation; Expo Go is insufficient for Android remote push.
+
+The actual mobile-client/API/database suite verifies default values, strict validation, private headers, owner/staff/session isolation, persisted reads from another session, an actual staff review honoring opt-out, category suppression/re-enabling, deduplication, preserved inbox history and logout rejection. Mobile UI regressions cover EN/BS loading/retry, failed draft retention, duplicate taps and late/401 responses. The existing claim-verification fixture adds the mobile account lookup; staff verification/release logic is unchanged.
